# =============================================================================
# SECTION 3: REGIONAL REGULATORY COMPLEXITY INDEX (RCIndex)
#
# The RCIndex operationalises institutional barriers to homeownership at the
# county level. Three indicators are drawn from the KHS County Government
# Questionnaire (Section cg of the 2023/24 KHS instrument):
#
#   R1 = Average building permit processing time (weeks) — variable cg3
#        Higher values indicate greater administrative friction.
#
#   R2 = Building application rejection rate = 1 − (cg4b / cg1b)
#        Proportion of received applications that were not approved.
#        One data anomaly (Samburu county: cg4b > cg1b) is corrected
#        by clipping the rejection rate to [0, 1].
#
#   R3 = No ratified building bylaws indicator (binary)
#        = 1 if county has NOT ratified revised Code 95 building bylaws
#        = 0 if ratified. Derived from cg11 (0 = not ratified, 1 = ratified).
#
# All three indicators are standardised to mean 0, unit variance before PCA.
# The first principal component is extracted from the correlation matrix of
# the standardised indicators across all 47 Kenyan counties.
# The raw PC1 score is normalised to [0, 1] for interpretability.
# A higher RCIndex indicates a more complex institutional environment.
# =============================================================================

